    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d413">

                <pb facs="0562" n="548" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg548"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.6362/8–245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Braden</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-18T13:00:00-04:00">August 18, 1945—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1105. Urtel 1737 Aug 2<anchor n="90" xml:id="d413-f1"/> and 1809 Aug 9. Dept has
                    been able to obtain removal of embargo on coal shipments to Argentina and it is
                    possible to ship 20,000 tons per month through Dec.</p>
                <p>Rather than start shipments gratuitously the Dept wishes to inform you that
                    shipments can be arranged and will be started when you advise the Dept that it
                    is desirable to do so.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
